From ca1034abb32a1877f6567e947463f0a641c4c4f1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Mrinohk <5554998+Mrinohk@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Mon, 12 Oct 2026 12:43:44 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 26/31] cuda : fp16 expert GEMM for MoE prompt processing on
 sm_60

sm_60 has no dp4a, so MMQ's int8 dot products are emulated: the q4_K / q5_K expert matmuls of prompt processing ran
at ~2.5 TFLOPS and were ~60% of prefill GPU time on Qwen3.6-35B-A3B. New path in front of MMQ for MUL_MAT_ID of
q4_K / q5_K experts (GGML_CUDA_P60_MEGA=1; GGML_CUDA_P60_MOE_GEMM=0 disables it):
- mm_ids_helper sorts the (token, slot) pairs by expert;
- their src1 rows are gathered once as fp16;
- one block turns the expert bounds into a tile list on the device (no host sync);
- a block computes 64 rows x 64 pairs of one expert: per 64-wide K step the weights are dequantized into shared
  memory as k-pairs (half2), so one 128-bit load gives 4 rows or 4 pairs; HFMA2 over the step, fp32 accumulation.

test-backend-ops MUL_MAT_ID matches the CPU backend for all q4_K / q5_K cases. 256 experts, 8 used, 1536 tokens:
q4_K gate (K 2048): 9833 -> 3588 us (7.2 TFLOPS); q5_K down (K 512): 10920 -> 3662 us.
2x P100, llama-bench -ub 1536: pp4096 1009 -> 1454 t/s, pp512 670 -> 859 t/s.
Wikitext KLD vs the stock ub=1 base at -ub 512: 0.00446 (stock MMQ 0.00526), same top token 97.24% (97.08%) -
fp16 activations instead of int8.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5
